{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\n# keep only the violated interpretation as the single submission element\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\nd['interpretations']=[i]\nd['sources'] += [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"truncate_conflict\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1522,\\\"end_line\\\":1553,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1236,\\\"end_line\\\":1241,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n]\ni['source_ids']=[s for s in i['source_ids']] + [\\\"truncate_conflict\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\"]\ni['answers']={\n \\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-gap-0\\\": i['answers'][\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-gap-0\\\"],\n \\\"a8b8d696ac934beda1434a93b5d7758f-gap-1\\\": i['answers'][\\\"a8b8d696ac934beda1434a93b5d7758f-gap-1\\\"],\n \\\"1ed9540f22fe4fa9bef3b3bda88e22e8-gap-2\\\": {\n   \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Answered at construction time, retained receipt pending. The construction-time run of the dual-majority probe reached every step: A restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs held the stale {A,B} configuration while its log held the newer {A,B,C} entry; with B partitioned, AddVoter E returned no error and the silently-created {A,B,E} entry committed on A plus the promoted, caught-up nonvoter E (A commit index 11 >= entry index 11, entry type LogConfiguration, and E held the same entry), while B stayed at index 10 with its old belief. B and C then elected B in term 4 while A was still leader in term 3 (two concurrent leaders over the same log with disjoint support {B,C} vs {A,E}), and after healing, A's entry at index 11 became a LogNoop of term 4 instead of the committed configuration entry, i.e. a committed entry was truncated on the node that had committed it. Source: the new configuration enters the commitment on append (raft.go 1236-1241), and appendEntries clears a conflicting suffix (raft.go 1522-1553).\\\",\n   \\\"resolved\\\": False}}\ni['limitations']=[l for l in i['limitations'] if 'live-quorum' not in l]\ni['limitations'] += [\n \\\"The dual-majority consequence (two concurrent leaders and truncation of the committed entry) is claimed from a construction-time run only; its retained receipt is requested in this update, and the earlier build-failure experience is why the harness is self-contained and was re-verified inside an isolated copy of the captured tree.\\\",\n \\\"In that probe the partitioned side elects its leader with 3s election timeouts (reloaded to keep the restarted leader from losing the first election), so the interval is seconds; the ordering it demonstrates does not depend on those particular values.\\\",\n \\\"No control variant is included: with the flag off the leader's configuration is current, so the same AddVoter is a single-server change and the two-server change that creates the disjoint majorities cannot arise.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\necho written\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
