e node that had committed it. Source: the new configuration enters the commitment on append (raft.go 1236-1241), and appendEntries clears a conflicting suffix (raft.go 1522-1553).\\\",\n   \\\"resolved\\\": False}}\ni['limitations']=[l for l in i['limitations'] if 'live-quorum' not in l]\ni['limitations'] += [\n \\\"The dual-majority consequence (two concurrent leaders and truncation of the committed entry) is claimed from a construction-time run only; its retained receipt is requested in this update, and the earlier build-failure experience is why the harness is self-contained and was re-verified inside an isolated copy of the captured tree.\\\",\n \\\"In that probe the partitioned side elects its leader with 3s election timeouts (reloaded to keep the restarted leader from losing the first election), so the interval is seconds; the ordering it demonstrates does not depend on those particular values.\\\",\n \\\"No control variant is included: with the flag off the leader's configuration is current, so the same AddVoter is a single-server change and the two-server change that creates the disjoint majorities cannot arise.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\necho written\"","aggregated_output":"written\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_dual_majority_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"truncate_conflict\\\",\\\"vote_config_checks\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Four in-process nodes at protocol version 3 with 300ms heartbeat/election/lease: A and B are bootstrapped as voters {A,B}; A snapshots, adds E as a caught-up nonvoter, adds C as a voter (config {A,B,C} plus nonvoter E), commits four commands. A is shut down and restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs=true so its in-memory configuration comes from the snapshot ({A,B}) while its log holds the newer {A,B,C} entry; the other three nodes get longer timeouts so the restarted leader wins back leadership. B is then partitioned from A (C is already absent from A's stale configuration, so A replicates to nobody but E), and A issues one AddVoter E. Observations: whether that change commits and with whose acknowledgement, each side's configuration and log tail, who leads each side and in which term, and the content of A's log at the created entry index before and after the partition is healed.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"E is a caught-up nonvoter before the change, which is what lets the silently-created {A,B,E} configuration commit with A and E alone once B is partitioned; this is ordinary use of AddNonvoter followed by AddVoter.\\\",\\\"Restarting the leader with RestoreCommittedLogs=true is the documented configuration already established by the earlier receipts; nothing else about the cluster changes.\\\",\\\"The partition is applied by disconnecting the in-memory transports in both directions, which is a real partition for all Raft traffic (AppendEntries, heartbeats, votes).\\\",\\\"Both sides keep following the protocol: A leads the {A,B,E} configuration with E's acknowledgements, and B and C campaign under their own {A,B,C} configuration after their election timeout.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No control variant: with the flag disabled the leader's configuration is current, so the same AddVoter adds a single server and the two-server change cannot arise; that is a source-level statement (nextConfiguration over the current configuration) rather than an execution.\\\",\\\"No disk faults or message loss; the only partition is the one applied explicitly.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"nodes\\\":4,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"leader_lease_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"other_side_election_timeout_ms\\\":3000}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real snapshot, real AddNonvoter catch-up, real AddVoter, real commits, graceful shutdown and restart of the leader on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances, real transport partition and real healing. The log, snapshot metadata and configurations all come from those operations; the harness never fabricates entries or configuration state.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"silent_change\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_type_at_x\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"LogConfiguration\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_leaders\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"silent_change\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_type_at_x\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"LogConfiguration\\\"}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed_entry_truncated\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry that was committed under the configuration recorded in the logs must not be replaced after the partition heals.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"old_side_elected\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"old_leader\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_leaders\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_still_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"At most one leader may exist for a given log: the old-configuration side must not elect a leader while the new-configuration side still leads.\\\"}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
